# Statistics Methods for Continuous Outcomes

## The Didgeridoo study

To discuss statistical methods for continuous outcomes, we use data from the didgeridoo study (@didgeridoo). In this RCT, participants with obstructive sleep apnea were randomized either to didgeridoo lessons with daily practice or to a waiting list for such lessons (control arm).

The primary endpoint is the Epworth Sleepiness Scale (ESS), a measure of daytime sleepiness on a scale from 0 (not sleepy in any situation) to 24 (very likely to fall asleep in all situations). We have data on this outcome at baseline (`epworth1`) and at 4 months (`epworth2`). (The data have been simplified for this tutorial.)

```{r didgeridoo-clean, echo = TRUE, message = FALSE}
library(tidyverse)
theme_set(theme_bw(base_size = 12))
library(gtsummary)

